        "created_at": 1794506288.6442504
      },
      "rev_n_3_212fc2_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_212fc2_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_212fc2",
        "thought_text": "Since N is small (up to 10^5), a simple loop is efficient enough and less prone to off-by-one errors in mathematical range calculations.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506288.6442585
      },
      "rev_n_4_46fbc4_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_46fbc4_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_46fbc4",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through each digit length from 1 up to the number of digits in N. For each odd length, add the count of numbers with that length that are less than or equal to N, being careful to cap the count at N if the current length equals the total digits of N.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1235274246270070534",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506305.6939633
      },
      "rev_n_5_d05832_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_d05832_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_d05832",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the total count of numbers with odd digit lengths in the full range [1, 10^k - 1] for relevant k, then subtract the count of numbers with odd digit lengths in the range [N+1, 10^k - 1] if N falls within a specific block, effectively using a complement approach.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1235274246270070534",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506305.6939895
      },
      "rev_n_6_afeb50_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_afeb50_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_afeb50",
        "thought_text": "Directly construct the answer by summing 9 * 10^(2k) for all valid k where the full block of odd-length numbers fits entirely below N, and then add the partial count for the specific odd-length block containing N.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1235274246270070534",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506305.6939995
      },
      "rev_n_4_46fbc4_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_46fbc4_1",
        "node_id": "n_4_46fbc4",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2 (revised): Iterate through each digit length from 1 up to the number of digits in N. For each odd length strictly less than the total digits of N, add the full count of numbers with that length. If the total number of digits is odd, add the count of numbers from the start of that digit range up to N (inclusive), rather than adding N directly.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1235274246270070534",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_4_46fbc4_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_e3bf8b45cf",
        "created_at": 1794506324.0596216
